INT. TAXIDERMY SHOP BACK OFFICE - NIGHT

Glass eyes in drawers. A stuffed heron on the filing cabinet. A desk lamp.

CONSTANCE BELLWETHER-OKAFOR (50s, shop owner, tweed) sits behind the desk. Across from her, INSPECTOR ARTHUR LINDQVIST (60s, bowler hat on his knee) leans forward.

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
Miss Bellwether-Okafor, the dead man was your partner.

CONSTANCE
He was, Inspector.

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
And you were the last to see him.

CONSTANCE
I locked up at six. He was alive then.

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
Alive and in a temper, the clerk says.

CONSTANCE
He was always in a temper.

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
About what?

CONSTANCE
The heron.

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
The heron.

CONSTANCE
He wanted to sell it. I did not.

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
To whom?

CONSTANCE
A collector. A man who pays in cash.

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
Name?

CONSTANCE
He never gave one.

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
Convenient.

CONSTANCE
For him, perhaps. Not for me.

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
Do you own a revolver, madam?

CONSTANCE
I own a skinning knife and a very good sense of humor.

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
The first I've seen. The second I'm waiting for.

CONSTANCE
Then you will wait a long time.

He taps his hat. She straightens a pen. The heron stares at both.

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
Tell me about the safe.

CONSTANCE
There is no safe.

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
There is a safe-shaped hole in your wall.

CONSTANCE
Is there?

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
Behind the heron.

CONSTANCE
I never look behind the heron.

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
Perhaps you should.

The door opens. A tall young man steps in, soaked, a package under his arm.

ELLIOTT FAIRWEATHER-NGUYEN (20s, delivery boy, cap dripping) stops. He looks from one to the other.

ELLIOTT
Sorry. Parcel for Mr. Pennington.

CONSTANCE
Mr. Pennington is dead.

ELLIOTT
Oh. Then who signs?

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
I will. What is it?

ELLIOTT
Don't know. It's ticking.

Inspector Lindqvist and Constance look at each other. Then at the parcel. Then at the heron.

CONSTANCE
Put it down gently, young man.

ELLIOTT
Is it going to--

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
It's going to be fine. Probably.

Elliott lowers the parcel onto the desk. The ticking stops. Silence.

Constance lifts the lid. Inside, a brass pocket watch and a note.

CONSTANCE
(reading)
"Look behind the heron. Signed, Pennington."

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
He's been dead since six.

CONSTANCE
He mailed it at five.

Elliott takes off his dripping cap.

ELLIOTT
Should I go?

INSPECTOR LINDQVIST
No. Stand by the heron. Both of you.

They turn toward the bird. It stares back, patient.
